---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
---
<Base title="Partners" description="How NextGenergy works with manufacturers, integrators and mechanical contractors, and what we ask of them.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Company" title="We build with partners. We stay accountable for the result." lede="We qualify manufacturing partners against our factory acceptance protocols and integration partners against our commissioning plans, within the scope each contract defines." crumbs={[['/company/about', 'Company']]} />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid c3">
        <div class="card"><span class="num">Manufacturing</span><h3>Skid, manifold and CDU builders</h3><p>Build to our specification and FAT protocol. We witness or audit the factory test, hold the records against serial numbers, and remain the accountable integration lead for the assembled path in service.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><span class="num">Integration</span><h3>Rack integrators and mechanical contractors</h3><p>Deploy against our commissioning plan. Every field boundary they make or disturb is logged and re-tested. They get a plan that is countable; we get records that are complete.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><span class="num">Off-take</span><h3>Heat buyers</h3><p>District networks, greenhouse and aquaculture operators, industrial process users. We design the loop to their temperature window and meter the hand-off at the data-centre boundary.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="note" style="margin-top:2.5rem;max-width:70ch"><strong>Becoming a partner.</strong> Send us your FAT protocol or your commissioning checklist. We will tell you where it meets the <a href="/evidence/turnover">ten-boundary structure</a> and where it does not. That conversation is the qualification.</div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
